note.p:
A separate memorandum in the PSF–Subject file states that President Truman;
                    Secretary Acheson; Lovett; John Kenney, Deputy Director of MSA; Jack Gorrie,
                    Chairman of the NSRB; John Snyder, Secretary of the Treasury; Sidney Souers,
                    Special Consultant to the President; General Twining, Chairman of the JCS;
                    General Smith, Director of Central Intelligence; Commander M. D. Clausner, JCS;
                    James Lay, Executive Secretary, NSC; and S. Everett Gleason, Deputy Executive
                    Secretary, NSC, were present.
